{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short --ignored=matching | head -n 40; git diff --check; sed -n '1,100p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n!! .agent.last\n!! .agent.log\n!! cores/bench/generated/\n!! cores/bench/sim_build/\n!! cores/bench/test/test_alu_runner.result.xml\n!! cores/bench/test/test_decoder_runner.result.xml\n!! cores/bench/test/test_div_unit_runner.result.xml\n!! cores/bench/test/test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml\n!! cores/bench/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml\n!! cores/bench/test/test_reg_file_runner.result.xml\n!! formal/last_run-w3DjdfwjM.log\n!! formal/last_run-wRH8R17C2.log\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n# Bench load/store effective addresses\n\nEX adds forwarded `rs1` to the decoded, sign-extended I/S immediate and captures the 32-bit sum in EX/MEM under the existing stall enable. MEM uses the registered sum for the byte address, lane masks, load extraction, alignment traps, and word-aligned RVFI address. The bus address follows the sum even with both strobes low. The existing ALU and jump-link selection still supplies integer forwarding and writeback.\n\nThe LSU shares the base-plus-immediate addition already used for JALR. JALR still clears bit 0 when forming the redirect target. Bus consumers continue to qualify accesses with the request strobes.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- The requested Verilator lint command passed. All six cocotb suites passed. The new directed test checks both forwarding sources and priority, `2047` and `-2048` crossing 4 KiB boundaries, 32-bit wraparound, byte and halfword lanes, misalignment traps, stall stability, and direct address drive during idle cycles.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement ALTOPS checks on the first run.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` passed in a scratch build with `NRET=1`. Selftest and all three random programs matched the Python ISS with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark completed with both markers, no out-of-bounds access, and canonical CRCs. The champion and candidate both started at cycle 15,801 and stopped at cycle 4,543,561 for 4,527,760 timed cycles. Both printed `Correct operation validated.` and reported `seedcrc=0xe9f5`, `crclist=0xe714`, `crcmatrix=0x1fd7`, `crcstate=0x8e3a`, and `crcfinal=0xfcaf`.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 routed at 62.973, 68.323, and 68.323 MHz using 2,860 LUT4s and 676 registers. The 68.323 MHz median yields 150.90 iterations/s, up 19.23% from 126.56 iterations/s. Each worst setup path ends at `cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result`. The option 0 routed report shows `cpu/u_ex/reg_q.effective_addr_12_s0/Q` directly driving `dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s/ADA[13]` through a routing net.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
