{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,140p' formal/checks_si.cfg; sed -n '510,540p' tools/orchestrator.py; ls -l cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p1/impl/gwsynthesis\"","aggregated_output":"[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n\n    # 2. (V2) No Yosys synthesis: FPGA timing and area come from the vendor\n    # flow at the FPGA gate (tools/eval/gowin.py), and formal already\n    # elaborates the RTL.\n\n    # 3. Build bench ELFs (selftest + coremark). They are gitignored.\n    # Bench programs are shared across cores; no target-specific env needed.\n    bench = subprocess.run(\n        [\"make\", \"-f\", \"bench/programs/Makefile\", \"all\"],\n        cwd=worktree, capture_output=True,\n    )\n    if bench.returncode != 0:\n        return _fail(\"bench make\", bench)\n\n    # 4. Rebuild Verilator cosim binary against the worktree's RTL.\n    # _build_cosim_env reads cores/<target>/core.yaml's nret to pick the\n    # NRET preprocessor value (1 or 2). main.cpp's ch1 drain is gated by\n    # `#if NRET >= 2`, so an nret=1 core (no `_1` ports) compiles cleanly.\n    from tools.eval.cosim import _build_cosim_env\n    build_env = _build_cosim_env(worktree, target=target) if target else None\n    build = subprocess.run(\n        [\"bash\", \"test/cosim/build.sh\"],\n        cwd=worktree, capture_output=True,\n        env=build_env,\n    )\n    if build.returncode != 0:\n        return _fail(\"cosim build\", build)\n    return (True, \"\")\n\ndef _read_notes(worktree: str) -> str:\n    p = Path(worktree) / \"implementation_notes.md\"\ntotal 1824\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2    6995 Nov 23 06:10 core_bench.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2    3795 Nov 23 06:10 core_bench.prj\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 1796199 Nov 23 06:10 core_bench.vg\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2   41248 Nov 23 06:10 core_bench_syn.rpt.html\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2    7580 Nov 23 06:10 core_bench_syn_resource.html\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2    1682 Nov 23 06:10 core_bench_syn_rsc.xml\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
