red selector for the alternate path.\\nSelect between those registered addresses in the existing correction\\ncycle. A fence refetch selects PC+4. An older deferred-branch miss\\nretains its saved address pair and selector and overrides younger EX\\ncorrection. Keep the existing EX and MEM correction latencies, queue\\nrebasing, and wrong-path store, divider and retirement suppression.\\n\\nFor a deferred branch, register byte comparisons directly from raw\\ndata-memory lanes and the nonmatching operand. Compare each potential\\nlane against its matching byte for word, halfword and byte accesses.\\nCarry the o\n…[13299 of 16371 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:043cb2acd1ed0b77]…\n63 MHz** median clears the 102.98 MHz threshold. At the measured cycle count it gives **312.39 CoreMark iterations/s**, up **7.23%**. The timed wrapper used 6,161 logic cells, 2,160 registers, 72 distributed RAM cells, and eight block RAMs. Replay accounted for 32 distributed RAM cells and four block RAMs.\n\nGowin repacked the inferred payload and steering address arrays into two block RAM primitives per parity, so the physical block boundaries differ from the RTL arrays. The direction and transfer flags retained fabric register outputs. Fully distributed steering and a mapping with separate physical payload blocks both produced lower medians.\n\ntimestamp 2026-11-23T08:58:05.902519Z\nslot 1\nround_id 14\nlesson - 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-002-r14s1 (improvement, +7.23%): Separating replay payload from PC steering, with fabric registers for cold direction and transfer flags and parallel high-tag and sampled-row checks, lifted median Gowin Fmax from 98.445 to 105.563 MHz at the same 3,379,213 stalled CoreMark cycles.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
