{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short --untracked-files=all && git check-ignore -v cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,125p' formal/checks-deep.cfg && sed -n '1,105p' formal/checks_si.cfg\"", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\tcores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Substitutes M-ext mul/div/rem with\n# simpler XOR-of-add/sub formulas so bitwuzla solves them inside the\n# 20-step BMC budget (rvfi.rst §7.6 \"Alternative arithmetic operations\").\n#\n# IMPORTANT — what this DOES and DOES NOT prove:\n#   ✓ proves: M-ext bypassing, operand routing (rs1/rs2 -> unit -> rd),\n#             stall/forwarding behavior on mul/div, all I-base arithmetic\n#             and trap discipline.\n#   ✗ does NOT prove: the actual MUL/DIV/REM arithmetic is correct.\n#     The DUT and the spec both implement the same XOR substitute under\n#     this define, so a wrong real multiplier can still pass formal here.\n#\n# M-extension arithmetic correctness is covered separately by:\n#   1. test/t