{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --numstat && git diff --check && nl -ba implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"5\t0\tcores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n25\t3\tcores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n10\t33\tcores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n16\t13\tcores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n     1\t# Register data-memory request controls in EX\n     2\t\n     3\tEX uses the forwarded base and immediate to compute a two-bit address sum in parallel with the full effective address. The two-bit sum also supplies JALR alignment. EX/MEM captures the shifted byte mask, alignment fault, aligned-request pending bit, and separate aligned read and write qualifiers under the existing data-bus hold.\n     4\t\n     5\tMEM qualifies the registered request bits with EX/MEM validity. A valid misaligned access retires with the trap flag set, zero RVFI memory masks, and writeback disabled. MEM still extracts and extends loads from the returned word and replicates store data across byte lanes. The existing EX/MEM hold keeps request address, write data, and enables stable, and MEM/WB still prevents duplicate retirement during the hold.\n     6\t\n     7\tThe pipeline regression now includes an upper-halfword access whose forwarded address calculation carries from bit 0 into bit 1. It also keeps the data bus unready during idle cycles to check that misaligned accesses retire without waiting for the bus.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Local verification\n    10\t\n    11\t- Verilator lint passed for regular RTL and `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`.\n    12\t- Co-simulation passed selftest and three random programs with ready and stalled buses. Stalled CoreMark matched the canonical CRCs and completed ten iterations in 3,965,757 timed cycles.\n    13\t- Single-retire formal, cocotb, and Gowin timing are in progress.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
