{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git branch -a --list \\\"*r9s1*\\\"; git log --all --oneline --grep=\\\"r9s1\\\"; rg -n 'hyp-20261123-002-r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c 1-3100; tail -8 \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/bench-pair-formal.log\"; tail -12 \"$TMPDIR/bench-pair-timing-b.log\"'", "aggregated_output": "9a35487 log: hyp-20261123-002-r9s1 regression\n27:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261123-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Put a registered head on the fetch queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 245.62 CoreMark iterations/s at 97.408 MHz over\\n3,965,757 marker-window cycles. In the median Gowin placement, the\\nEX/MEM bypass-to-queue-occupancy path ties the queue-head-to-register-file\\npath. The circular queue uses a four-way packet read before decode and\\nresets several control registers directly from the forwarded branch\\ncomparison. Both paths can be shortened at the fetch-to-decode boundary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion scores 245.62 CoreMark iterations/s at 97.408 MHz over\\n3,965,757 marker-window cycles. In the median Gowin placement, the\\nEX/MEM bypass-to-queue-occupancy path ties the queue-head-to-register-file\\npath. The circular queue uses a four-way packet read before decode and\\nresets several control registers directly from the forwarded branch\\ncomparison. Both paths can be shortened at the fetch-to-decode boundary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the four-packet capacity and empty-queue fall-through. Give the\\noldest queued packet a dedicated head register, with three circular\\nslots behind it. Drive decode from the registered head or the current\\nbus response. Promote the oldest rear packet into the head only when the\\nhead is consumed. Use a live response to replace a consumed lone head,\\nor to fill an empty head if decode is blocked. Use registered capacity\\nfor normal fetch advance. Keep the head stable while decode is held,\\nand let ready bus responses fill the available rear slots.\\n\\nUse the already registered EX recovery choice to make the queue appear\\nempty and suppress the younger sampled ID/EX valid before it can execute,\\nforward, issue a divide or retire. Advance or enqueue the first corrected\\nresponse in that cycle, then commit fresh queue state. Preserve the\\nexisting full-address retry and readiness behavior. Form the folded\\nprediction index for each normal, target and fall-through PC before\\ntheir selection. Read the existing 64-entry direction state as four\\n16-entry banks using the same index and training rules. This preserves\\nthe prediction decisions and keeps the selected-PC XOR off the fetch\\nfeedback path.\\n\\nA scratch prototype routed at 97.571, 99.446 and 99.446 MHz. The\\nmedian placement's worst path ends at the EX/MEM ALU result. Stalled\\nCoreMark validated in 3,965,757 marker cycles, yielding 250.76 iter/s\\nwith the measured median. At that cycle count, replacement requires\\na median above 101.889 MHz.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the four-way packet read with a registered front packet and a three-slot rear FIFO. Use the registered correction to discard stale packets. Precompute the candidate PC hashes and bank the direction table without changing its logical state or training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Register the advancing direction mismatch and mask the sampled ID/EX valid before EX or any forwarding and haz\nSBY  5:07:56 [insn_srli_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:11 (11)\nSBY  5:07:56 [insn_srli_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY  5:07:56 [insn_srli_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY  5:07:56 [insn_srli_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nSBY  5:07:58 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:04  Checking assertions in ste