{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_157","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git diff --stat && sed -n '1,100p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           |  51 ++++++++----\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |  17 ++--\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       |  82 ++++++++++--------\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv    |  22 +++--\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv       |   7 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv       | 111 +++++++++++++------------\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv      | 106 +++++++++++++-----------\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 170 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 8 files changed, 395 insertions(+), 171 deletions(-)\n# Registered load forwarding and branch recovery\n\nDecode allows a load to use a preceding LW as its base at displacements 0, 1, and 2. It records both raw source matches, including the unused rs2 field. EX keeps the ordinary forwarded operands available for a trapping producer. MEM/WB captures the raw load word alongside the formatted result, and RVFI uses the qualified result for each matching source.\n\nGowin could not infer the data block RAM with a mux after the address registers. The implementation selects the ordinary address or response upper bits at the request register's input. The address port is driven directly by that register. A three-bit sum supplies the low bits and carry. A carry suppresses both strobes for one cycle and rewrites the request register's upper bits using the saved raw word. The pipeline holds the response during correction and holds the corrected request through backpressure. The regular width-dependent alignment check covers the final byte address.\n\nDeferred branches compare the registered formatted load result against the nonmatching EX operand, byte lane by byte lane. MEM accounts for signed ordering, reversed operands, two qualified matches, and the ordinary comparison when a load traps. EX and MEM resolve into a shared registered correction boundary with MEM priority. In the correction cycle, fetch ignores the discarded queue contents, younger side effects are gated by age, and speculative divider work is canceled. A deferred miss retires in the slot vacated by the squash.\n\nPredictor training captures the next counter state at MEM resolution. The pending state bypasses to both lookup and a following update to the same index. The folded PC index, initialization, saturation policy, and visibility of updates are preserved.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- All six cocotb runners passed, including 58 pipeline cases. The directed tests check exact bus and RVFI packets for consecutive paired loads, each eligible displacement, crossings and 32-bit wraparound, producer and consumer misalignment, stalls, interlock exclusions, and correction into a divide.\n- The unchanged `bash formal/run_all.sh` single-channel gate passed all 53 checks on the selected RTL, including register consistency and ready-bus liveness. No RTL retries were needed for that run.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest and the three randomized programs with and without bus stalls, and validated stalled CoreMark.\n\n## Gowin timing and CoreMark\n\nThe shared recovery register variant routed at 92.153, 102.059, and 102.059 MHz across the three placements. The median placements were limited by the saved branch operand through the MEM comparator into the registered recovery select, with ordinary address generation close behind. Placement 0 reported 4,955 logic cells, 1,515 registers, four block RAMs, and two DSPs.\n\nStalled CoreMark validated all five canonical CRCs in 3,829,362 marker cycles. That saves 29,395 cycles relative to the champion. The 102.059 MHz median gives 266.52 iterations/s, about 2.98% above 258.81 iterations/s. The measured cycle savings and frequency fall short of the hypothesis's projected improvement.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
