{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_131","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && ls -l cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 2669 Nov 23 10:47 cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Sequential companion replay\n\nMEM completion supplies a base PC one word before each candidate instruction. The companion banks accept only validated ALU, load, and store instructions. Each lookup compares the sampled row, bank parity, and full high tag. Reset and FENCE.I clear both replay tables, and each bank masks same-edge read and write collisions.\n\nThe four-entry queue reserves two entries from registered occupancy before admitting a companion. A ready bus can bypass an empty queue as before. A primary replay enters the queue. Both rear writes sample fixed positions from the registered tail and its rotation. If the primary fills the head and the companion goes to the rear, the read pointer skips the unused primary position. An empty queue can sample the companion into the head while the primary bypasses. The acceptance logic publishes the resulting entries. Correction flushes the queue and takes priority over both admissions.\n\nFetch computes the two sequential word offsets, wraps, and direction indices separately. The companion match and initial capacity select between the sequential candidates in parallel with branch prediction. The core still retires one instruction per cycle on RVFI channel 0.\n\nBoth replay tables use the same validity circuit. Distributed RAM stores per-row bits, and one resettable bit per group hides stale rows. The first write after a clear resets the other bits in its group. The hazard unit compares the live and queued register sources in parallel and selects the resulting dependency signals to shorten the path into the queue.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint and all eight bench cocotb runners passed. The directed tests cover bus and replay primaries, full-queue holds, head promotion, redirects, the two page-wrap cases, alias replacement, same-edge collisions, and FENCE.I with a modified companion.\n- Five-program co-simulation passed. Stalled CoreMark validated all canonical CRCs. Markers at cycles 12,404 and 3,349,251 give **3,336,847 marker cycles**, a reduction of 42,366 cycles from the champion.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured **86.207, 99.090, and 99.090 MHz**. The median gives **296.96 iterations/s** and falls below the 109.0348 MHz replacement threshold. The two median placements were limited by the path from the instruction source through fetch into queue occupancy. The divider and ALU also appeared among the slowest paths.\n- The single-retire formal gate recorded **52 of 53 checks passing**, including cover, liveness, retirement uniqueness, and illegal-instruction checks. Bitwuzla was still checking the `reg_ch0` assertion at step 20. No counterexample was reported.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
