{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_126","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git status --short --untracked-files=all; cat implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n D cores/bench/rtl/loop_replay.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/replay_table.sv\n?? cores/bench/test/test_replay_table.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n# Successor replay\n\nThe fetch stage now uses two synchronous 256-row block RAM banks in place of loop capture. Each 72-bit row stores the full word PC, instruction bits `[31:2]`, the low ten bits of the direct target's word address, and page-local branch and JAL qualifiers. MEM registers one update per eligible completion. It reuses the direct target already carried from EX for deferred branch resolution, so an untaken branch records its actual target. Traps, SYSTEM, fences, and JALR are excluded.\n\nThe banks read the registered normal PC and its sequential successor. The even bank increments the pair index when the normal PC is odd. Registered validity suppresses same-row read/write collisions. FENCE.I clears both validity maps and suppresses the pending write on its correction edge, after the older store completes.\n\nA ready bus response can fall through to decode. On a stall, an exact hit with queue space advances the PC and enqueues its instruction and prediction together. Tag comparisons qualify publication and PC writes. PC data selection uses bus readiness and the predicted direction. The existing EX and deferred MEM correction paths validate replayed transfers, and the correction cycle uses the bus.\n\nGowin initially mapped wide tag equality onto a carry chain. Two-bit comparison groups let it map the full tags in parallel. Registering the direction-counter index with the PC kept the existing hash and counters while removing the hash from the lookup path. The queue uses one occupancy bit per filled position to shorten the push path. The full-queue hold and four-entry depth are preserved.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint and all seven cocotb suites passed, including 55 pipeline cases. Directed tests cover a taken prediction from a previously untaken branch, JAL and untaken replay, ready bus priority, queue holds, stalled deferred correction, alias eviction, both banks' read/write collision masks, training eligibility, and FENCE.I following a stalled code store.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest and all three random programs with ready and stalled buses. Stalled CoreMark passed the canonical CRCs, memory bounds, and marker validation at **3,379,213** cycles, a **7.62%** reduction from the champion.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured **92.068, 98.445, and 98.445 MHz**. `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` reproduced the **98.445 MHz** median and scored **291.33 CoreMark iterations/s**, **7.16%** above the champion. Placement 0 used 5,952 logic cells and eight block RAMs including the benchmark wrapper. The slower option was limited by EX forwarding into the ALU. The median's worst reported path runs from a replay RAM output to a fetch PC register.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retire checks on the final RTL. The first run hit a Yosys parser error on `$bits(replay_row_t)`. Using `$bits` on a signal of that type resolved it, and the retry passed. The formal wrapper holds both buses ready. Directed tests and stalled co-simulation exercise replay under backpressure.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
