{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_146","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- cores/bench/rtl | cmp - \"$TMPDIR/bench-target-replay-v5.diff\"; sed -n '\"'1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; rg -c 'DONE \\\\(PASS' formal/last_run-wvuIRY2Ds.log; rg 'DONE \\\\((FAIL|ERROR)' formal/last_run-wvuIRY2Ds.log\"","aggregated_output":" cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv           |  13 ++-\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv           |  54 +++++++----\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv          |  10 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/replay_table.sv       | 109 ++++++++++++++-------\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py     | 174 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n cores/bench/test/test_replay_table.py | 174 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----------\n 6 files changed, 414 insertions(+), 120 deletions(-)\n# Predicted-target instruction replay\n\nThe instruction rows now hold instruction and PC tag bits only. MEM sends the existing eligible completion to the replay table, which writes the ordinary parity bank, the target copy, and the 512-slot asynchronous successor RAM in parallel. Each successor entry packs a 10-bit page-local target word, a conditional-branch bit, and the static direction. A JAL uses the unconditional taken encoding. Conditional branches use the existing trained bimodal counter when available.\n\nThe registered normal PC indexes the successor RAM. Its target word launches the synchronous target read every cycle. The accepted normal fetch direction sets a one-cycle target preference. Each synchronous read registers its slot address and same-slot write collision. The sampled slot and upper tag together check the full PC, and a single current-slot validity lookup qualifies the selected response. The sampled slot check also prevents an unwritten row's zero tag from borrowing PC zero's validity. The held and sequential reads handle retries. A ready bus response wins, and recovery uses the bus. Reset and FENCE.I clear availability and suppress all replay writes.\n\nDirected tests cover the first stalled target cycle at both instruction parities, live and replayed branch sources, a cold target miss and retry, an unwritten slot with a zero tag, alias eviction, collisions on all three reads, reset and FENCE.I, a full queue, and EX and deferred MEM corrections with a primed target. The pipeline tests check RVFI retirement order, exact successor PCs, and memory side effects.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint and all seven cocotb suites passed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest and three random programs with ready and stalled buses. The canonical stalled CoreMark run passed CRC, bounds, and marker checks in **3,361,505** marker cycles for 10 iterations.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured **94.989, 99.529, and 99.529 MHz**, for a **99.529 MHz** median and **296.08 CoreMark iterations/s**. This falls below the stated 102.44 MHz replacement threshold. The median placement's slowest path runs from an even replay bank to fetch queue occupancy. Placement 0 used 6,736 logic cells, 136 LUT-RAMs, and 10 block RAMs, including the benchmark wrapper.\n- Local formal has passed 52 of 53 checks. The single-retire `reg_ch0` solver is still running.\n52\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
