{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_124","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"stat -c '%y %n' .agent.last .agent.log && date && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"2026-11-23 10:19:45.109176287 +0100 .agent.last\n2026-11-23 10:46:38.224478036 +0100 .agent.log\nMon Nov 23 10:46:42 CET 2026\n# Loop-exit predictor\n\nMEM sends the folded branch PC, resolved outcome, and displacement sign once per valid nontrapping completion. This includes load-dependent branches and deferred misses whose RVFI packet retires on the following cycle.\n\nFetch retains 64 rows. Each row records a six-bit saturating taken run, the previous completed run, trip confidence, and two bits of agreement with the static backward-taken direction. Capture, metadata sampling, and transition are registered. If an older sample or publication targets the sampled row, the younger update starts with cold metadata, including weak fallback agreement. The publication edge writes both the row state and the sign-relative override. The trained map, overrides, and in-flight valid bits reset synchronously. Untrained rows take their metadata from the cold state.\n\nFour banks read the override in parallel. Each bank keeps its own four-bit row register under a synthesis hierarchy boundary, and every replica uses the PC word write enable, including correction. The folded bank bits are decoded into one-hot form before selection and registered separately. The default and flipped paths each prepare the next word and folded index from the live or replay steering. Correction owns the next PC and index when asserted.\n\nThe pipeline tests cover matching trips, early exits, overruns, saturation, both same-row conflict distances, and fallback predictions through folded aliases with opposite displacement signs. They check the retired PC sequence through stalled loads and instruction replay.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed in the standard and ALTOPS builds. All seven cocotb suites passed, including 59 pipeline cases.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and all three random programs with ready and stalled buses. Stalled CoreMark passed all canonical CRCs in 3,363,240 marker cycles.\n- The first formal run passed 52 of 53 checks. `pc_fwd_ch0` found consecutive retired PCs of zero despite a reported next PC of four. Yosys had elaborated the generated packed-struct successor array as a narrow signal. Named successor bundles with a shared selection function removed that elaboration issue. The retry passed 52 checks, including PC continuity. The `reg_ch0` solver was still running at depth 20 at the last check and had produced no counterexample.\n- Gowin routed at 93.274, 95.376, and 95.376 MHz, for a 95.376 MHz median. The reported paths include all four row-register replicas. Replay tag matching through the PC word write enable limited option 0. The existing data-BRAM-to-late-branch comparison limited options 1 and 2.\n- The result reduced stalled CoreMark by 15,973 marker cycles and scored an estimated 283.58 iterations/s, below the 312.39 iterations/s champion. A block-RAM metadata trial and a trial that folded reset into the shared PC word enable both routed slower in option 1.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
