{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml; sed -n '1,155p' formal/checks_si.cfg; sed -n '1,160p' formal/wrapper_si.sv; nproc; cat /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max\"", "aggregated_output": "name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 76.948\n  lut4: 3082\n  ff: 701\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261122-002-r4s1\n  updated: '2026-11-22T23:13:20.616345Z'\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n// riscv-formal wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. \n…[1834 of 4906 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2e60263a8f8e8175]…\nn the core's IO under nret=1.\n        .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid),\n        .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order),\n        .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn),\n        .io_rvfi_trap_0     (rvfi_trap),\n        .io_rvfi_halt_0     (rvfi_halt),\n        .io_rvfi_intr_0     (rvfi_intr),\n        .io_rvfi_mode_0     (rvfi_mode),\n        .io_rvfi_ixl_0      (rvfi_ixl),\n        .io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0 (rvfi_rs1_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0(rvfi_rs1_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0 (rvfi_rs2_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0(rvfi_rs2_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_rd_addr_0  (rvfi_rd_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0 (rvfi_rd_wdata),\n        .io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0 (rvfi_pc_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0 (rvfi_pc_wdata),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_addr_0 (rvfi_mem_addr),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0(rvfi_mem_rmask),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0(rvfi_mem_wmask),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0(rvfi_mem_rdata),\n        .io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0(rvfi_mem_wdata)\n    );\n\nendmodule\n20\ncat: /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max: No such file or directory\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
