{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor path in sorted(Path('.tmp/agent-logs').glob('impl.*-r4s[01].log')):\n    print(path.name)\n    for line in path.open():\n        try:\n            event = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n        item = event.get('item', {})\n        if event.get('type') == 'item.completed' and item.get('type') == 'agent_message':\n            print(item.get('text', '')[:2300])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"impl.hyp-20261122-001-r4s0.log\nI’ll check the bench worktree and verification targets, then implement the EX operand selector and run the local gates.\nLint and cosim passed, and stalled CoreMark matched the canonical CRCs in 4,527,760 marker cycles. The first routed median was 68.222 MHz, below the 71.47 MHz replacement threshold. I’ll inspect the critical path and tune the EX selector mapping.\nThe ALU result path added several LUT levels after operand selection. A parallel result selector raised the routed median to 72.564 MHz, and all 53 formal checks and cosim passed on that candidate. I’ll check whether the forwarding path alone can meet the threshold before settling on the final RTL.\n[Implementation notes](</srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-001-r4s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md>)\n\nThe four-way EX selector uses Gowin’s `syn_keep` to group the bypass terms. It routed at a **72.896 MHz median** and scored **161.00 CoreMark iterations/s**, up **6.69%** at the same **4,527,760 marker cycles**.\n\nLint, all 53 formal checks, all six cocotb suites, and cosim passed.\nimpl.hyp-20261122-002-r4s1.log\nI’ll inspect the bench worktree and test entry points, then implement decode-side forwarding and run the verification gates.\nThe first routed build moved the worst setup path to the divider in all three placements. Its 71.342 MHz median is just below the 71.47 MHz replacement threshold. RVFI cosim passed, and I’m checking whether a simpler encoding of the same decode and execute logic can clear the margin.\nThe revised build scores 169.95 CoreMark iterations/s, up 12.62% from the champion at the same 4,527,760 timed cycles. All six cocotb suites and RVFI cosim passed. The final formal run is still checking register consistency.\nImplemented decode-side operand selection in `cores/bench`. Verilator lint, all 53 ALTOPS formal checks, all six cocotb suites, and RVFI cosim passed.\n\nGowin routed at 75.007, 76.948, and 76.948 MHz. The median was 3.481 MHz below the scratch prototype and cleared the replacement threshold. CoreMark scored **169.95 iterations/s**, up **12.62%** from the champion at the same 4,527,760 timed cycles.\n\n[Implementation notes](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-002-r4s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
