le and its greater-than-15 flag for the existing\\nleading-nibble update. Test that flag directly from the original\\ndivisor bits in parallel with negation. A negative divisor has magnitude\\n1 through 15 exactly when bits 31:4 are all ones and its low nibble is\\nnonzero.\\\n…[68524 of 71596 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bddd7a5bd5d91fe6]…\n.96, \"delta_pct\": -4.94, \"vs_baseline\": 2350.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 99.09, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3336847, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6223, \"ff\": 1744, \"seeds\": [86.207, 99.09, 99.09], \"perturbations\": [[0, 86.207, 11], [1, 99.09, 10], [2, 99.09, 10]], \"lutram\": 104, \"bsram\": 12, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_local_30_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.6, \"arrival_ns\": 16.894, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T10:04:13.320413Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 15, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-002-r15s1 (regression, -4.94%): Companion replay with registered rear write slots saved 42,366 stalled CoreMark cycles, and the same-cycle path from live instruction bits through admission logic to queue occupancy capped median Gowin Fmax at 99.090 MHz, more than offsetting the cycle savings.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
