\n156-cell path runs through forwarding and the EX ALU to the data-memory\\naddress cone. The ALU places signed and unsigned division and remainder\\noperators on the same result path as ordinary address arithmetic. A shared\\niterative divider should remove most of that depth and reduce LUT use. A\\nbaseline Verilator trace with both bus stalls enabled reproduced 4491485\\nmarker-\n…[26021 of 29093 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a7ce5e68bb8b59f4]…\nx_mhz\": 57.304, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4527760, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2880, \"ff\": 644, \"seeds\": [59.33, 57.304, 57.304], \"perturbations\": [[0, 59.33, 15], [1, 57.304, 15], [2, 57.304, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -11.855, \"arrival_ns\": 22.15, \"logic_cells\": 15, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T22:30:51.499814Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r2s1 (improvement, +24.76%): Registering multiply partial products and divide magnitudes in a separate EX/MEM lane and clearing ID/EX validity on redirects shortened the data-memory address and hazard feedback paths enough to outweigh a one-cycle interlock for MEM/WB forwarding when either raw source field matched the late destination.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
