{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md && cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r1s0 (regression, +536.14%): Moving combinational DIV/REM off the EX address path into a shared restoring divider raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.442 to 34.631 MHz, and the seven extra cycles per operation left the CoreMark cycle count unchanged because all divides retired outside the timed interval.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r1s1 (improvement, +736.96%): Two cascaded radix-4 steps with parallel subtracts kept EX division to nine cycles at a median routed core Fmax of 45.562 MHz, leaving one cycle for a load-use or redirect bubble within the ten-cycle ready-bus RVFI liveness bound.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +7.67%): A 64-entry bimodal table and early JAL target selection in IF avoided taken-transfer bubbles and cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.7%, with the combinational DIV/REM path limiting median Gowin Fmax to 5.47 MHz and throughput to 13.05 iterations/s versus 101.44 for the multicycle-divider winner.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r2s0 (regression, +17.06%): With a combinational instruction response, driving `io_imemAddr` and the IF/ID PC tag from the resolved EX target removed redirect bubbles and cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 7.9%, with the PC advancing to target plus four on acceptance and saving the target for retry when either bus blocked acceptance.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r2s1 (improvement, +24.76%): Registering multiply partial products and divide magnitudes in a separate EX/MEM lane and clearing ID/EX validity on redirects shortened the data-memory address and hazard feedback paths enough to outweigh a one-cycle interlock for MEM/WB forwarding when either raw source field matched the late destination.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r2s2 (regression, +14.05%): Predicting branches and JAL in IF with a shared target and one-bit EX recovery cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.7%, and the path from forwarding through the EX ALU to the data-memory address remained critical, leaving 48.479 MHz median Fmax behind the 57.304 MHz pipelined EX design that won on throughput.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
