{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nls=[json.loads(l) for l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor d in ls:\n if d.get('category') in {'structural','micro_opt'} or 'r3s' in d.get('id',''):\n  print(d.get('id'),d.get('category'),d.get('title'),list(d))\n  for k,v in d.items():\n   if k in {'hypothesis','implementation_notes','result','timing'}:\n    print(k,str(v)[:10000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-af44a5c micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench ['id', 'title', 'category', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'round_id', 'slot']\nimplementation_notes \nhyp-20261122-001-r1s0 micro_opt Fold the EX divider into six registered iterations ['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The bench baseline scores 12.12 at 5.442 MHz. Its reported 199.837 ns,\\n156-cell path runs through forwarding and the EX ALU to the data-memory\\naddress cone. The ALU places signed and unsigned division and remainder\\noperators on the same result path as ordinary address arithmetic. A shared\\niterative divider should remove most of that depth and reduce LUT use. A\\nbaseline Verilator trace with both bus stalls enabled reproduced 4491485\\nmarker-bracketed cycles with canonical CRCs and retired zero divide or\\nremainder instructions inside the bracket. Both retired DIVUs were outside it.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one unsigned restoring divider in EX.\\nOn launch, capture the forwarded operands, take unsigned magnitudes for signed\\noperations, and save the result kind and signs. Run six radix-2 steps per\\nclock for six clocks using a 36-bit dividend stream with four leading zeros.\\nEach step shifts in a dividend bit, takes a 33-bit trial remainder through a\\nborrow-producing subtraction of the divisor, and shifts the quotient bit into\\nthe vacated low end of the stream. Select and s\n…[40773 of 43845 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ea0ffa4d3bd4916c]…\nte lookup, rewritten instructions including traps and a divide, simultaneous bus stalls, exactly-once training and wrong-path store suppression.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with zero warnings. All six cocotb suites passed, including 25 pipeline cases.\n- Single-retire ALTOPS formal passed all 53 checks on the first run, including ten-cycle ready-bus liveness.\n- Co-simulation matched the self-test and three random RVFI traces on ready and stalled buses. Stalled CoreMark passed the canonical CRC and marker checks at 4,251,388 marker cycles, 6.1% fewer than the champion.\n- Gowin placements reported 58.051, 59.747 and 59.747 MHz. The 59.747 MHz median exceeds the 56.281 MHz replacement threshold. The scored throughput was 140.54 iterations/s, up 11.0% over the champion. The hypothesis estimated 12%.\n- Gowin reported 3,422 logic cells and 746 registers. The IF table inferred 32 distributed RAM macros. The worst placed paths end in dmem address logic, with recovery to the fetch PC close behind.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
