{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\"|hyp-20261122-002-r2s1|hyp-20261122-001-r2s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [(lambda d: print(d.keys(), str(d)[:12500]))(json.loads(l)) for l in sys.stdin]'\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']) {'id': 'hyp-20261122-003-r1s2', 'title': 'Predict direct control transfers in fetch with a bimodal table', 'category': 'predictor', 'motivation': 'The benchmark core fetches sequentially until EX resolves a taken transfer.\\nIts unregistered IF/ID bundle means each nonsequential transfer discards one\\nfetch slot. Predicting hot loop branches and direct jumps can reuse those\\nslots for useful work. The measured 156-cell critical path is in forwarding\\nand the ALU, so the new fetch logic has timing headroom if its fanout stays\\nlocal.\\n', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The benchmark core fetches sequentially until EX resolves a taken transfer.\\nIts unregistered IF/ID bundle means each nonsequential transfer discards one\\nfetch slot. Predicting hot loop branches and direct jumps can reuse those\\nslots for useful work. The measured 156-cell critical path is in forwarding\\nand the ALU, so the new fetch logic has timing headroom if its fanout stays\\nlocal.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"In IF, predict decoded conditional branches with 64 two-bit saturating\\ncounters indexed by pc[7:2] XOR pc[13:8]. Predict backward branches taken\\nand forward branches not taken on untrained entries. Initialize each entry\\nweakly toward its first outcome, then train once per advancing, valid,\\nnontrapping conditional branch. When prediction and training share one\\nentry in a cycle, prediction uses the pre-update state. Predict JAL taken\\nand resolve JALR in EX.\\nUse a shared PC-relative adder for B and JAL immediates and require the\\nspeculative target to be four-byte aligned and below 0x00100000. Select\\nthe predicted successor only when the correspo\n…[36917 of 39989 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:32ceed95ec010d7e]…\nrgument selects the single-retire interface declared in `core.yaml`.\\n- Gowin placements measured 44.842, 48.479, and 48.479 MHz. The 48.479 MHz median and 4,190,281 stalled marker cycles yielded 115.69 iterations/sec, 14.0% above the 101.44 iterations/sec champion.\\n\\n## Timing and area\\n\\nThe local implementation used 3,326 logic cells and 821 registers, above the scratch measurements of 3,136 and 819. Placement option 0 cleared the 44.462 MHz replacement threshold by 0.380 MHz. Its worst setup path ran through forwarding and the EX ALU to the data address logic.\\n', 'timestamp': '2026-11-22T22:30:04.324961Z', 'slot': 2, 'round_id': 2, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r2s2 (regression, +14.05%): Predicting branches and JAL in IF with a shared target and one-bit EX recovery cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.7%, and the path from forwarding through the EX ALU to the data-memory address remained critical, leaving 48.479 MHz median Fmax behind the 57.304 MHz pipelined EX design that won on throughput.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
