{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith(('r9s1','r10s1','r11s1')):\n  print(d['id'],(d['implementation_notes'] or '')[:7800])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261123-002-r9s1 \nhyp-20261123-002-r10s1 \nhyp-20261123-002-r11s1 # Implementation notes\n\nEX registers the active lanes, byte gather selects, and narrow sign source with the effective address. The lane decode uses the low two bits of the forwarded base-plus-immediate sum, which also supplies the JALR alignment check. MEM gathers writeback data from the two 16-bit response groups and reports the active lanes in RVFI `mem_rmask`.\n\nThe deferred branch compares raw bytes against the other operand positioned in those groups. EX registers an equal and less-than pair for each byte, gives inactive lanes the identity relation, and registers a leading pair for extension and signed ordering. MEM combines the pairs in significance order and applies source orientation and branch polarity. The accepted load's formatted WB value supplies the matching RVFI operands. A trapping load selects the ordinary forwarded comparison, and two matches compare equal. The existing stage enables hold the descriptor and branch through a stalled response.\n\nThe retained version uses one-hot gather selects and parallel comparator operand routing. A compact gather variant measured 95.158 MHz median, with 52 of 53 formal checks passed and `reg_ch0` still solving near the local deadline. The one-hot version completed the full gate.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel checks on the first run of the retained RTL.\n- All six cocotb test runners passed. The new pipeline cases cover each legal lane, zero and all-ones extension boundaries, every branch condition, both source positions, double matches with stale register data, stalled responses, and misaligned loads.\n- Co-simulation passed selftest and all three random trace ELFs with and without bus stalls and validated the stalled CoreMark CRCs. CoreMark used 3,858,757 cycles between the markers.\n\n## Timing\n\n| RTL | Gowin option 0 | Option 1 | Option 2 | Median |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Champion | 89.262 MHz | 99.867 MHz | 99.867 MHz | 99.867 MHz |\n| Registered load lanes | 93.412 MHz | 92.039 MHz | 92.039 MHz | 92.039 MHz |\n\nThe worst path moved from the data BRAM and load formatter to fetch page selection in option 0 and the divider recurrence in options 1 and 2. At the validated marker cycle count, the median gives 238.52 CoreMark iterations/s, 7.84% below the champion.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
