a stall. If the load\n  traps, bypass the lane flags and certify equality from the ordinary\n  forwarded sources in EX. A double match also bypasses the flags and\n  compares equal when the load completes. For a single accepted match,\n  equality requires both the lane reduction and the ext\n…[1152 of 4224 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fe8a3d92477eb202]…\nom the adjacent-load interlock. Preserve the existing raw-source dependency rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Route the raw dmem word to EX with the older load's registered byte offset, width, signedness, and access qualification.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Position the nonmatching forwarded operand by width and register the masked equality flags. Fold the extension check, double match, and trapping-load fallback into registered eligibility for equality.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve the bypassed equality condition from the registered flags while preserving bus stalls, prediction updates, recovery priority, and RVFI values.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise every legal byte and halfword lane, equal payloads with opposing extension prefixes, both source positions, double matches, and trapping and stalled loads. Retain the ordered-branch correctness cases and check their restored one-cycle interlock.\"\nMon Nov 23 06:24:21 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
