{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    r=json.loads(l)\n    print(r['id'], r.get('category'), r.get('fitness'), r.get('fmax_mhz'), r.get('seeds'), r.get('title'))\n    if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261122-002-r1s1','hyp-20261122-002-r4s1']:\n        print(r.get('critical_path'), r.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-af44a5c micro_opt 12.12 5.442 [5.14, 5.442, 5.442] Baseline retest for cores/bench\nhyp-20261122-001-r1s0 micro_opt 77.1 34.631 [34.91, 34.631, 34.631] Fold the EX divider into six registered iterations\nhyp-20261122-002-r1s1 structural 101.44 45.562 [46.428, 45.562, 45.562] Move DIV and REM into a bounded multicycle execute unit\n{'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -16.539, 'arrival_ns': 26.833, 'logic_cells': 15, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} # Bench multicycle divider\n\n`div_unit.sv` implements DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with two cascaded radix-4 steps per update cycle. Each step uses three parallel widened subtraction results to choose a quotient digit and the next remainder. The result transfers directly to EX/MEM on the eighth update. If the consumer is blocked on that cycle, the divider holds the final step's inputs so the result and operands stay stable. Divide by zero and signed overflow use the same schedule as other operands. ALTOPS uses the specified formulas on the captured operands with the same controller.\n\nEX keeps the instruction in ID/EX and captures the forwarded operands separately for the divide and RVFI. Issue waits for older data memory traffic to advance. EX/MEM receives bubbles while the divider runs, so older instructions can retire. The completed divide transfers once and forwards through EX/MEM. Base integer and multiply operations retain their one-cycle EX latency.\n\nThe divider tests live in `test_div_unit.py` so the clocked divider and the combinational ALU can be tested as separate Verilator top modules. `core.sv` includes `core_pkg.sv` when the build has yet to read it, which lets the requested alphabetical glob lint command resolve pipeline types.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS modes.\n- The stock single-channel `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed 53 checks on the first run, including liveness and all four divide and remainder instructions\n…[1519 of 4591 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c41caa5ec56daf9b]…\n Predict direct transfers in fetch with a direction-only recovery check\nhyp-20261122-001-r3s0 micro_opt 150.9 68.323 [62.973, 68.323, 68.323] Generate load and store addresses outside the execute ALU\nhyp-20261122-002-r3s1 structural 150.9 68.323 [62.973, 68.323, 68.323] Give loads and stores a dedicated registered address path\nhyp-20261122-003-r3s2 predictor 140.54 59.747 [58.051, 59.747, 59.747] Predict the next fetch with a tagged last-successor buffer\nhyp-20261122-001-r4s0 micro_opt 161.0 72.896 [69.836, 72.896, 72.896] Select register operands with one execute bypass mux\nhyp-20261122-002-r4s1 structural 169.95 76.948 [75.007, 76.948, 76.948] Resolve execute operand selection in decode\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_31_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.div_magnitude_2_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.332, 'arrival_ns': 18.626, 'logic_cells': 72, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']} \nhyp-20261122-003-r4s2 predictor 159.16 67.414 [68.723, 67.414, 67.414] Predict page-local direct transfers with registered recovery\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
