{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-550 && rg --files --hidden -g AGENTS.md -g '\"'!**/.git/**'\"' . .agents && true\"", "aggregated_output": "1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-af44a5c\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.83\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Fold the EX divider into six registered iterations\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The bench baseline scores 12.12 at 5.442 MHz. Its reported 199.837 ns,\\n156-cell path runs through forwarding and the EX ALU to the data-memory\\naddress cone. The ALU places signed and unsigned division and remainder\\noperators on the same result path as ordinary address arithmetic. A shared\\niterative divider should remove most of that depth and reduce LUT use. A\\nbaseline Verilator trace with both bus stalls\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Fetch resolved redirect targets in the execute cycle\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 101.44 CoreMark iterations per second.\\nIts IF/ID interface is combinational. A taken branch or jump in EX\\ncurrently discards the sequential response and spends an edge\\nloading the target into the fetch PC before requesting that target.\\nThe resolved target is already available to select the instruction\\naddress in that cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench champion s\n8:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Generate load and store addresses outside the execute ALU\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 126.56 iterations/s at a median Gowin Fmax of\\n57.304 MHz over 4,527,760 timed CoreMark cycles. Its reported 22.15 ns\\npath runs from the register file through ID and the execute ALU to data\\nmemory. Loads and stores always add a forwarded rs1 to a signed 12-bit\\ndisplacement. Their address currently passes through the general ALU\\noperand and result selection and the jump-link\n11:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Select register operands with one execute bypass mux\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 150.90 iterations/s at 68.323 MHz and takes\\n4,527,760 timed CoreMark cycles. The worst setup path in the reproduced\\nplacement-option-0 report starts at the register-file block RAM and\\ncrosses the write-first ID bypass, EX forwarding, and the integer ALU.\\nOne selector in EX can choose among all four data sources once ID\\ncaptures its write-first data and hit bits separately.\\n\",\n14:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261123-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Resolve each four-bit divide digit with parallel trial subtractions\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current bench champion scores 169.95 CoreMark iterations/s at a median\\nGowin Fmax of 76.948 MHz. Its reported worst path runs from the divider's\\nquotient register through the final two radix-4 steps to the EX/MEM divide\\nmagnitude register. Each four-bit update makes its second subtraction wait\\nfor the first digit's remainder mux. Earlier profiling found no divides or\\nremainders betwe\n17:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261123-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Fetch resolved targets with a deferred PC increment\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion spends one fetch slot on each taken branch, JAL or\\nJALR. CoreMark takes 4,527,760 timed cycles at a median 88.028 MHz. The\\nround-2 same-cycle redirect recovered 7.9% of the cycles on an older core.\\nIts update computed the target plus four in the redirect cycle. Deferring\\nthat increment and simplifying EX's branch and link-write logic shortens\\nthe redirect path for the current core.\\n\"\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
