{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261123-002-r7s1|hyp-20261123-002-r6s1|hyp-20261123-002-r8s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; ds=[json.loads(l) for l in sys.stdin]; [print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"),d.get(\\\"critical_path\\\")) for d in ds if d[\\\"id\\\"] in [\\\"hyp-20261123-002-r7s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261123-002-r6s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261123-002-r8s1\\\"]]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-002-r6s1 {'motivation': 'The champion takes 4,527,760 marker-window cycles at a median 88.028 MHz.\\nA stalled CoreMark trace counted 294,425 taken conditional branches and\\n49,367 JALs in that window. Each currently waits for a clock edge to put\\nits resolved target on the instruction bus. Retiming the fetch increment\\naddresses the target-to-next-PC feedback of the earlier same-cycle redirect\\nattempt and can trade a small clock loss for fewer cycles.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Drive the current instruction request and its IF/ID PC tag from the\\nresolved EX target for a valid, aligned, taken branch or JAL. Use the\\ncombinational response as the next instruction when both stages can\\nadvance. Keep request address selection independent of both bus-ready\\ninputs. A data-memory hold retains the older instruction and commits no\\nredirect. If EX advances while instruction memory is stalled, remember\\nthe exact target for retry. JALR continues to squash the sequential\\ninstruction and put its resolved target in registered fetch state.\\n\\nRepresent fetch state as a 30-bit word-address base plus a registered\\nadvance bit. An accepted request records the request address and sets\\nadvance. A redirect that needs retry, or a JALR, records the target with\\nadvance clear. Apply the word increment from registered state with\\nparallel lower-bit reductions, keeping it off the EX target path. Resolve\\nconditional branches with four byte-level equality and unsigned less-than\\ncomparisons. A byte can determine the ordering when all higher bytes\\nmatch. For signed comparisons with different operand signs, use the sign\\nof rs1. Select equality or ordering with funct3 bit 2 and invert for\\nfunct3 bit 0 after legal branch decode. For alignment, use immediate bit 1\\nfor direct transfers and compute sum bit 1 from the low two operand bits\\nfor JALR. Qualify fast link writes with jump alignment. Keep architectural\\nRVFI successors, traps, data-memory side effects, late-result interlocks,\\nand single-channel retirement. A ready-bus dir\n…[10469 of 13541 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c708447297d16f3e]…\ns, yielding 235.08 iterations/s\\nat the measured median. The gain was 2.54%. Replacement at that cycle\\ncount requires a median above 95.097 MHz. The new median timing limit\\nruns from MEM/WB forwarding to fetch-queue head control, with a narrow\\ndivider recurrence path close behind. Recheck both in the scored placements.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 3, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/div_unit.sv', 'description': 'Dispatch on divisor magnitude, use a 24-bit direct radix-16 recurrence for narrow divides, and pipeline three full-width digit rounds for wide divides.'}, {'file': 'test/test_div_unit.py', 'description': 'Add signed and unsigned vectors on both sides of the width cutoff and retain cycle-count, zero-divisor, signed-overflow, and held-completion checks.'}]} {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_local_31_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_20_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.298, 'arrival_ns': 16.592, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
