{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"hyp-20261123-00[123]-r[89]s[012]\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; keys=\\\"id title outcome cycles fitness fmax_mhz critical_path hypothesis implementation_notes\\\".split(); [print(json.dumps({k:r.get(k) for k in keys},indent=1)) for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n \"id\": \"hyp-20261123-001-r8s0\",\n \"title\": \"Select radix-16 divider residuals with a binary mux tree\",\n \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n \"cycles\": 3965757,\n \"fitness\": 245.62,\n \"fmax_mhz\": 97.408,\n \"critical_path\": {\n  \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_16_s0\",\n  \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/head_q_0_s1\",\n  \"slack_ns\": -6.081,\n  \"arrival_ns\": 16.376,\n  \"logic_cells\": 17,\n  \"modules\": [\n   \"clock_ibuf\",\n   \"cpu/u_ex\",\n   \"cpu/u_if\"\n  ]\n },\n \"hypothesis\": {\n  \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 229.25 CoreMark iterations/s at a median\\nGowin Fmax of 90.915 MHz over 3,965,757 timed cycles. Its reported\\nworst path runs from the divider quotient register to the EX/MEM\\ndivide-magnitude register. Each radix-16 update gates all 16\\ncandidate residual words with a decoded one-hot digit and combines\\nthem with a wide OR reduction. A split-borrow prototype reduced the\\ncarry depth but routed at 70.478 MHz, motivating a change to residual\\nselection with the existing native subtract chains.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Use a four-level binary mux tree to select the residual from the\\nexisting candidate differences. At each node, use the fit bit of\\nthe lowest candidate in the upper half as the select. Pair adjacent\\nresiduals first using odd-numbered fits, then use fits 2/6/10/14,\\nthen 4/12, and finally 8. The fit bits are monotone because they\\ncompare the same trial against increasing multiples of an unsigned\\ndivisor magnitude, with the existing widened-multiple guard. Each\\nselection therefore directs the tree to the greatest fitting digit.\\nThe direct fit selects remove the adjacent-fit decode from the\\n32-bit residual path. Keep the existing one-hot quotient encoding\\non its separate four-bit path.\\n\\nPreserve the nine-cycle EX schedule, leading-nibble handling,\\ndirect final transfer, signed result handling, ALTOPS expressions,\\nand result stability while EX/MEM is held. Validate arithmetic\\nusing the existing digit-boundary, overflow, divide-by-zero, and\\nheld-completion tests, and retain the single-retire formal checks.\\nA SAT miter \n…[33617 of 36689 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7ef84cf993615fa8]…\nbuses. The canonical stalled CoreMark run validated the required UART result and all five CRCs in 3,790,292 marker cycles.\\n- The first formal run stopped at a Yosys parse error on a type-form `$bits`. Using the packet signal as the operand fixed elaboration. On the selected RTL, `formal/run_all.sh` passed 51 of 53 checks, including ready-bus divider liveness. The configured Bitwuzla runs for `pc_fwd_ch0` and `reg_ch0` remained open. The same bounded register check passed independently with ABC bmc3. The forward PC check had no result or counterexample within the implementation window.\\n\\n## Gowin timing\\n\\n| Placement | Fmax |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| 0 | 89.198 MHz |\\n| 1 | 94.621 MHz |\\n| 2 | 94.621 MHz |\\n\\nThe 94.621 MHz median yields 249.64 iterations/s. The cycle count meets the 3.80 million target. The routed design falls short of both 98.0 MHz and the 256.92 iterations/s replacement threshold. The limiting path runs from the registered recovery address through direction prediction to the fetch queue.\\n\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
