{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; rows=[json.loads(s) for s in sys.stdin]; print(list(rows[-1])); [print(str({k:v for k,v in row.items() if k in [\\\"id\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"outcome\\\",\\\"timing\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\"]})[:1700]) for row in rows]'\"", "aggregated_output": "['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\n{'id': 'hyp-20261122-002-r1s1', 'title': 'Move DIV and REM into a bounded multicycle execute unit', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The bench baseline places at a median 5.442 MHz. Its 199.837 ns worst path crosses forwarding and the execute ALU before reaching the data-memory path, and the mapped path contains 156 cells. The four combinational division and remainder operators feed the same result mux as every base ALU instruction and effective address. The path depth makes this arithmetic the strongest candidate for the current frequency limit. An RV32IM reference run of the canonical 2K, ten-iteration, -O3 CoreMark build matched all expected CRCs and retired zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions among 2,922,016 instructions between the timing markers.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Move DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU out of the combinational ALU into a single blocking divider attached to EX. On issue, capture the forwarded operands, operation and sign flags. Advance the unsigned quotient and remainder four dividend bits per cycle using two cascaded radix-4 digit steps. Each step uses parallel widened subtracts and their borrow bits to select the residual for the largest fitting multiple of the divisor. In the eighth update cycle, select the quotient or remainder, apply sign correction and transfer directly to EX/MEM. Preserve the specified zero-divisor and signed overflow results. Use the same issue, wait and completion schedule under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, substituting the specified operand formulas for the arithmetic so the formal gate exercises the same interlocks. The eight extra cycles leave one cycle for a preceding load-use or redirect\n…[14334 of 17406 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:86fd3d2c7b4f6c8e]…\ncycle saved\\n110,028 cycles. Its median Fmax fell to 86.361 MHz, and splitting the\\ncomparators exposed the data RAM-to-recovery path directly.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Let a legal BEQ/BNE dependent on the immediately preceding load enter\\nEX while the load enters MEM. In ID tag each source that matches the\\nload's nonzero destination. Preserve normal forwarding on the other\\nsource and retain both ordinary operand selections as a fallback if the\\nolder load traps. Keep the existing interlocks for other consumers.\\n\\nIn EX prepare the branch's target and fall-through, the other forwarded\\noperand and the fallback equality predicate. Hold both stages while the\\nolder load is unready. When the branch reaches MEM, compare against the\\naligned and extended value already in MEM/WB using four parallel byte\\ncomparisons. Treat two sources supplied by that load as equal. If the\\nload trapped, use the prepared equality from the ordinary operands.\\nUse the same qualified load value to repair the tagged RVFI source\\nvalues, \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
