fers in fetch with a direction-only recovery check\nhyp-20261122-001-r3s0 micro_opt Generate load and store addresses outside the execute ALU\nhyp-20261122-002-r3s1 structural Give loads and stores a dedicated registered address path\n    The bench champion scores 126.56 CoreMark iterations/s at a median Gowin Fmax of 57.304 MHz over 4,527,760 marker-window cycles. Its reported worst path reaches the data RAM through the integer ALU even though each effective address is just the forwarded base register plus a sign-extended immediate. The general operand and result selection logic still couples the RAM address to the integer\n…[4665 of 7737 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c3aef5c15e5407ce]…\ncontrol. A stalled CoreMark retirement trace also shows about 135,000 adjacent load-to-BEQ/BNE dependencies inside the markers. Each pair is eligible for the current late-result interlock, even though the branch needs only an equality predi\nhyp-20261123-003-r10s2 predictor Pipeline prediction bits for loop replay in the fetch queue\nhyp-20261123-001-r11s0 micro_opt Compare raw load lanes before selecting branch bytes\nhyp-20261123-002-r11s1 structural Predecode load lanes before the data response\n    The champion scores 258.81 CoreMark iterations/s in 3,858,757 marker cycles at a median 99.867 MHz. The reproduced critical path starts at data BRAM and runs through the load formatter to a registered branch byte-less flag. The effective byte offset, width and signedness are available before the data arrives. A scratch prototype that registered formatter lane selects in EX/MEM validated CoreMark and matched the cycle coun\nhyp-20261123-003-r11s2 predictor Predict short loop iterations with two resident replay banks\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
