ise\\\\ncompete with the datapath for routing slack.\\\\n\\', \\'hypothesis\\': \"Learn two resident page-local loops of up to 16 contiguous words from', 'expected_impact': \"{'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'medium'}\", 'changes': \"[{'file': 'rtl/loop_replay.sv', 'description': 'Train two tagged loops from registered MEM observations and supply read-ahead replay packets from a shared synchronou\n…[1238 of 4310 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cdd8e2ae606e3532]…\nh completing instruction, including the resolved direction of deferred branches. A 32-word circular history tracks page-local sequential runs and identifies a span from the displacement of a short taken backward branch. Observations continue during a copy. The registered reader advances through the captured span before the writer can wrap onto it. One synchronous replay RAM holds both 16-word banks. Installation publishes the full head PC with the final write, prefers an empty bank before round-robin replacement, and protects the active bank or the matching idle head. Each bank', 'timestamp': '2026-11-23T07:03:54.367223Z', 'slot': '2', 'round_id': '12', 'lesson': \"- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-003-r12s2 (improvement, +5.04%): Pairing a dedicated fetch-queue head with registered recovery that masks ID/EX and also EX/MEM on a MEM miss removed combinational recovery feedback from the queue, raising two-bank loop replay's median Gowin Fmax from 96.875 to 99.444 MHz at roughly 3.658 million stalled CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
