{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; rows=sys.stdin.readlines(); print(len(rows)); [print(s.split(\\\":\\\",1)[0], {k:v for k,v in json.loads(s.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1]).items() if k not in (\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"results\\\",\\\"eval\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"notes\\\",\\\"gate_results\\\")}) for s in rows[-17:]]'\"", "aggregated_output": "14\n3 {'id': 'hyp-20261122-002-r1s1', 'title': 'Move DIV and REM into a bounded multicycle execute unit', 'category': 'structural', 'motivation': 'The bench baseline places at a median 5.442 MHz. Its 199.837 ns worst path crosses forwarding and the execute ALU before reaching the data-memory path, and the mapped path contains 156 cells. The four combinational division and remainder operators feed the same result mux as every base ALU instruction and effective address. The path depth makes this arithmetic the strongest candidate for the current frequency limit. An RV32IM reference run of the canonical 2K, ten-iteration, -O3 CoreMark build matched all expected CRCs and retired zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions among 2,922,016 instructions between the timing markers.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 50, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Remove the combinational DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU result arms and their ALTOPS substitutes from the fast ALU. Retain base integer and multiply operations.'}, {'file': 'rtl/div_unit.sv', 'description': 'Add the shared registered divider with two radix-4 digit steps per cycle, captured operands, signed correction and edge cases, ALTOPS arithmetic, and a result held until accepted.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Launch valid divides from forwarded operands, inject EX/MEM bubbles until the result can advance, and use the captured operands and divider result when advancing the original instruction. Clear pending state on reset.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the EX divide wait signal to the hazard logic while preserving normal EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding and single-channel RVFI.'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Hold the PC and ID/EX while the divider works. Keep older dmem backpressure higher priority and preserve normal memory and writeback advance during divider-only waits.'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Run division vectors against the clocked divider and pr\n…[39143 of 42215 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bc9aeeb72ca20a9b]…\n.'}], 'outcome': 'improvement', 'fitness': 312.39, 'delta_pct': 7.23, 'vs_baseline': 2477.48, 'fmax_mhz': 105.563, 'ipc_coremark': 3e-06, 'cycles': 3379213, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 6161, 'ff': 2160, 'seeds': [99.107, 105.563, 105.563], 'perturbations': [[0, 99.107, 13], [1, 105.563, 11], [2, 105.563, 11]], 'lutram': 72, 'bsram': 8, 'dsp': 2, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/divisor_q_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_3_s0', 'slack_ns': -5.09, 'arrival_ns': 15.384, 'logic_cells': 15, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}, 'logic_levels': 13, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None, 'timestamp': '2026-11-23T08:58:05.902519Z', 'slot': 1, 'round_id': 14, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-002-r14s1 (improvement, +7.23%): Separating replay payload from PC steering, with fabric registers for cold direction and transfer flags and parallel high-tag and sampled-row checks, lifted median Gowin Fmax from 98.445 to 105.563 MHz at the same 3,379,213 stalled CoreMark cycles.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
