ddress, store data and request controls stable\nacross data-bus backpressure, and complete the transaction once when\nready. Keep the load-use interlock, divide schedule, and single-channel\nretirement timing. This uses the existing EX/MEM boundary and adds zero\nissue or retirement bubbles.\n\nA three-file scratch prototype routed at 62.973, 68.323 and 68.323 MHz in\nthe three Gowin placements and used 2,860 logic cells and 676 registers.\nThe worst reported path in each placement terminated at the registered\ninteger ALU result. The stal\n…[4044 of 7116 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:68cfb54863505845]…\n> bool:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:155:    # Plain threads and blocking waits, no asyncio: agents run `make timing`\ntools/eval/gowin.py:158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:200:    \"\"\"`make timing TARGET=<core>`: the vendor timing the evaluator scores,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:214:                                wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\", options=opts)\ntools/eval/gowin.py:221:        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\nMakefile:1:.PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\nMakefile:83:\t@echo \"  make timing TARGET=v1   — Gowin Fmax and worst paths (placement option 0)\"\nMakefile:135:# FPGA timing and area come from the vendor flow, Gowin EDA\nMakefile:140:timing:\nbin\noss-cad-suite\nxpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
