MEM on an eligible EX match, MEM/WB on\\nan eligible MEM match alone, and the local value when neither matches. EX\\neligibility requires a valid fast result and the trap-adjusted register\\nwrite control. MEM eligibility uses the existing next MEM/WB reg_write\\nexpression, so a misaligned load cannot forward. Exclude x0 from both\\nmatches. Keep the write-first register-file path for the producer already\\nin WB and the interlock for late EX producers, including dependencies on\\nthe raw source fields reported by RVFI.\\n\\nFor integer ALU operands, register the local A and B values with PC and\\nimmediate selection already applied. Qualify each ALU bypass enable in ID\\nby whether that ALU operand actually uses the r\n…[27587 of 30659 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:71bfb0d053db4452]…\ning test exercises folded aliases, saturation, simultaneous lookup and update, and training around stalls. The predicted JAL-to-REMU retirement gap is nine cycles.\\n\\n## Local verification\\n\\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint passed. All 53 single-retire ALTOPS formal checks passed on the first run of the final RTL.\\n- All six cocotb suites passed. Co-simulation passed for self-test and three random RVFI traces in both stall modes. The stalled CoreMark run passed the canonical CRC and marker checks with no out-of-bounds access.\\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench` measured 4,227,283 bracketed CoreMark cycles, down 6.64%. Gowin placement options measured 83.248, 90.926, and 90.926 MHz. The median gives 215.09 iterations/s, up 10.63% from 194.42 iterations/s. Placement option 0 used 4,574 logic LUTs, 1,162 registers, and 40 distributed RAM blocks.\\n- Timing depends on placement. Option 0's longest path runs from a registered forwarding select to an IF recovery select. The median exceeds the 85.967 MHz acceptance threshold.\\n\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
