nk-write behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Drive decode acceptance into the fetch queue and route the decode head validity into hazard detection. Preserve the predictor update register and the memory and RVFI interfaces.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Qualify the existing late-result interlock with decode-head validity and export it independently of redirect. Keep dmem and divide holds and the redirect squash.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Update exact fetch sequences in the recovery-under-backpressure test for a decoupled front end. Check empty fall-through, full-queue hold and drain, simultaneous push and pop, and a queued late dependency. Keep retirement order, PC continuity, exact dmem requests, wrong-path store exclusion, redirect retry, and ready-bus latency assertions.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
