{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg --files --hidden -g AGENTS.md -g '\"'!**/.git/**'\"' . /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/formal/riscv-formal | head -60; sed -n '1,140p' formal/checks_si.cfg; ls -la cores/bench/rtl; cat cores/bench/core.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\ntotal 124\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 02:45 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 23 02:45 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  862 Nov 23 02:45 alu.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 9911 Nov 23 02:45 core.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 5917 Nov 23 02:45 core_pkg.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 8860 Nov 23 02:45 decoder.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 8501 Nov 23 02:45 div_unit.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 7929 Nov 23 02:45 ex_stage.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 1136 Nov 23 02:45 forward_unit.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 1217 Nov 23 02:45 hazard_unit.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 4669 Nov 23 02:45 id_stage.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 7464 Nov 23 02:45 if_stage.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 1317 Nov 23 02:45 imm_gen.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 5947 Nov 23 02:45 mem_stage.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  898 Nov 23 02:45 mul_reduce.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 1056 Nov 23 02:45 mul_unit.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 1664 Nov 23 02:45 reg_file.sv\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  614 Nov 23 02:45 wb_stage.sv\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 97.408\n  lut4: 4662\n  ff: 1427\n  coremark_iter_s: 3.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261123-001-r8s0\n  updated: '2026-11-23T01:44:40.893921Z'\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
