{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'\nfor line in open(p):\n r=json.loads(line)\n print(r.keys() if r['id'].endswith('r8s0') else '',end=''); print(r['id'], r['category'],r['title'])\n if r['id'].endswith(('r8s0','r8s1','r8s2','r6s1','r3s1')):\n  for key in ('hypothesis','implementation_notes','result','eval','metrics'):\n   if key in r:\n    v=r[key]\n    if isinstance(v,dict): v={k: str(i)[:1000] for k,i in v.items()}\n    print(key, str(v)[:7700])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-af44a5c micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench\nhyp-20261122-001-r1s0 micro_opt Fold the EX divider into six registered iterations\nhyp-20261122-002-r1s1 structural Move DIV and REM into a bounded multicycle execute unit\nhyp-20261122-003-r1s2 predictor Predict direct control transfers in fetch with a bimodal table\nhyp-20261122-001-r2s0 micro_opt Fetch resolved redirect targets in the execute cycle\nhyp-20261122-002-r2s1 structural Register M-extension results separately from fast execute\nhyp-20261122-003-r2s2 predictor Predict direct transfers in fetch with a direction-only recovery check\nhyp-20261122-001-r3s0 micro_opt Generate load and store addresses outside the execute ALU\nhyp-20261122-002-r3s1 structural Give loads and stores a dedicated registered address path\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The bench champion scores 126.56 CoreMark iterations/s at a median Gowin Fmax\\nof 57.304 MHz over 4,527,760 marker-window cycles. Its reported worst path\\nreaches the data RAM through the integer ALU even though each effective\\naddress is just the forwarded base register plus a sign-extended immediate.\\nThe general operand and result selection logic still couples the RAM\\naddress to the integer execute datapath and its bypass loop.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Give loads and stores a dedicated path to EX/MEM. Reuse the existing\\nJALR adder that computes forwarded rs1 plus the decoded immediate\\nmodulo 2^32. Register the unmasked sum as a byte address in its own\\nEX/MEM field under the existing stage advance condition. JALR continues\\nto clear bit zero on its redirect target. Drive the data-memory address\\ndirectly from the new field. The generic ALU operand muxes, ALU result\\nselector and link selection are outside this address path. The EX/MEM\\ninteger result continues to feed fast bypass and integer writeback.\\n\\nUse the registered effective address for alignment checks, load-byte\\nextraction, store masks, and RVFI aligned memory addresses. Preserve\\nfull-width wraparound, misalignment traps and side-effect suppressio\n…[20283 of 23355 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c0de8c234238abe8]…\nh kinds of branch exit, excluded words, and reset during\nactive replay. The tests check RVFI continuity and exact memory requests.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=12 bash formal/run_all.sh`\n  passed all 53 checks on this RTL with zero retries.\n- The bench cocotb suite passed, including all 42 pipeline cases.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest, the three random\n  programs, and CoreMark. CoreMark validated all five canonical CRCs.\n- CoreMark took **3,784,327 marker cycles** with imem and dmem stalls,\n  matching the prototype and reducing the champion's 3,965,757 cycles by\n  4.57%.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` measured 82.890, 90.678, and\n  90.678 MHz across Gowin placement options 0–2.\n  The **90.678 MHz median** yields **239.61 iterations/s**, 4.52% above\n  the champion. It is 0.068 MHz below the stated 90.746 MHz target and\n  0.938 MHz below the prototype median. The median placement's worst\n  setup path is in the divider.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
