{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261123-003-r[89]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; [print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"],d[\\\"critical_path\\\"]) for d in map(json.loads,sys.stdin) if d[\\\"id\\\"] in [\\\"hyp-20261123-003-r8s2\\\",\\\"hyp-20261123-003-r9s2\\\"]]' \"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-003-r8s2 # Short loop replay\n\n`cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv` captures accepted instruction-bus words in a\n16-entry circular window. A shifted mask tracks the uninterrupted run of\nreplayable responses. The direction predictor can start replay when a\nlegal, aligned, taken-predicted backward branch closes a complete\nsame-page span of 2–16 words.\n\nThe window registers its head read on the tail write edge and reads ahead\none word as each replay packet advances. Replay carries the original PC,\npredicts the tail taken and internal branches untaken, and parks the bus\nat the head. Queue backpressure holds the replay packet. The registered\nEX correction selects the bus address, makes the queue appear empty, and\ndiscards the previous capture run. The bus PC registers current and next\npage candidates independently of the sequential-wrap decision.\n\nThe capture mask restarts on any predicted-taken transfer, including a\nbranch whose target equals its fall-through. Replay is scoped to one\ninvocation. Jumps, SYSTEM, FENCE, and FENCE.I use the bus path, and\nre-entry captures fresh responses. The self-modifying code test checks\nthat a completed store followed by FENCE.I and a jump back into the loop\nsupplies the patched instruction on the next invocation.\n\n`cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py` updates the exact speculative fetch\nsequences in both data-stalled direction-miss cases. It also checks\nimem stalls throughout replay, a full queue under dmem stalls, the\n2-, 16-, and 17-word boundaries, page crossing and blocked wrap\ncorrection, both kinds of branch exit, excluded words, and reset during\nactive replay. The tests check RVFI continuity and exact memory requests.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=12 bash formal/run_all.sh`\n  passed all 53 checks on this RTL with zero retries.\n- The bench cocotb suite passed, including all 42 pipeline cases.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest, the three random\n  programs, and CoreMark. CoreMark validated all\n…[3044 of 6116 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bc3859404cdebb63]…\nys parse error on a type-form `$bits`. Using the packet signal as the operand fixed elaboration. On the selected RTL, `formal/run_all.sh` passed 51 of 53 checks, including ready-bus divider liveness. The configured Bitwuzla runs for `pc_fwd_ch0` and `reg_ch0` remained open. The same bounded register check passed independently with ABC bmc3. The forward PC check had no result or counterexample within the implementation window.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement | Fmax |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 89.198 MHz |\n| 1 | 94.621 MHz |\n| 2 | 94.621 MHz |\n\nThe 94.621 MHz median yields 249.64 iterations/s. The cycle count meets the 3.80 million target. The routed design falls short of both 98.0 MHz and the 256.92 iterations/s replacement threshold. The limiting path runs from the registered recovery address through direction prediction to the fetch queue.\n {'from': 'cpu/u_if/fallthrough_q_12_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/packets_q[3]_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.211, 'arrival_ns': 16.505, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
