{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; [print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d[\\\"hypothesis\\\"].get(\\\"hypothesis\\\", \\\"\\\")) for d in map(json.loads,sys.stdin) if d[\\\"id\\\"] in [\\\"hyp-20261123-003-r8s2\\\"]]' && ls -a /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261123-003-r8s2 Add a single 16-word loop replay buffer in IF. Record consecutive accepted\nbus responses in a circular window indexed by the low four word-PC bits.\nTrack the preceding run of sequential, replayable responses with a shifted\nvalidity mask indexed by the backedge's negative word displacement.\nReset it on redirect, a predicted nonsequential advance, or an excluded\nopcode. Allow straight-line integer, memory, and RV32M opcodes and legal,\naligned conditional branches. Keep jumps, SYSTEM, FENCE, and FENCE.I on\nthe bus path. When a legal, aligned, same-page backward conditional branch\npredicts taken and its complete 2-to-16-word span has been captured, record\nthe head PC and tail slot and enter replay as the branch word is written.\n\nReplay one saved word per cycle with queue space, independent of imem_ready.\nTag each word with its exact PC, predict the internal conditional branches\nnot taken, and predict the tail taken so the replay cursor wraps to the head.\nPark the instruction bus at the loop head and hold the replay cursor if the\nqueue has no space. EX checks each branch through the existing one-bit\nrecovery path. A mismatched tail or internal branch squashes younger\ninstructions and gives the registered correction address priority over\nreplay and any queued packet. Invalidate replay eligibility on recovery and\nreset. Record fresh words on each new invocation, so a FENCE.I between loop\ninvocations causes the new instruction stream to be fetched from the bus.\n\nRegister the replay window's output before selecting it for the fetch queue.\nAt loop entry read the head in parallel with writing the distinct tail slot.\nDuring replay read the successor in advance, and hold the registered packet\nduring backpressure. Precompute queue occupancy for a held and a consumed\nhead in parallel so decode acceptance only selects the next queue state.\nUse the registered recovery select to treat the queue as empty and drop\nreplay eligibility on the recovery cycle. Keep the EX decision off the\nreplay array. On the instruction-bus path, register both the current and\nnext sequential page candidates. Register the normal-page choice separately\nso the prediction and advance decision does not drive the upper-PC data\nregisters. Give the registered EX recovery addresses priority over both\nnormal-page candidates, including on a page wrap or blocked correction.\n\nThe retimed scratch prototype ran CoreMark in 3,784,327 marker cycles with\nall canonical CRCs, down 4.57%. Gowin placements measured 88.367, 91.616,\nand 91.616 MHz. The 91.616 MHz median exceeds the 90.746 MHz needed at that\ncycle count and yields 242.09 iterations/s, 5.60% above the champion.\nIn the existing direction-miss test, two data-stalled cases observe the\nnew speculative replay address sequence. Update the exact cycle-by-cycle\nfetch expectations for that sequence and retain the existing retirement,\ntrap, recovery retry, and memory request assertions.\nConfirm correctness, the marker count, and the median on the implementation.\n\n.\n..\nCORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\nLESSONS.md\ncore.yaml\nexperiments\ngenerated\nobj_dir\nrtl\ntest\nworktrees\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
