{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261123-001-r8s0\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys, json; [print(d[\\\"critical_path\\\"],d[\\\"perturbations\\\"],d[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"]) for d in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"","aggregated_output":"{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_16_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/head_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.081, 'arrival_ns': 16.376, 'logic_cells': 17, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']} [[0, 90.242, 12], [1, 97.408, 11], [2, 97.408, 11]] # Implementation notes\n\nThe radix-16 divider selects its 32-bit residual through four levels of binary muxes. Odd fit bits select each adjacent pair, then fits 2, 6, 10, and 14 select groups of four, fits 4 and 12 select groups of eight, and fit 8 selects the final residual. The separate four-bit quotient digit still uses the adjacent-fit one-hot encoding.\n\nThe implementation follows the proposed topology and preserves the native subtract chains, widened-multiple guard, leading-nibble step, nine-cycle EX schedule, direct final transfer, sign handling, and completion hold. The selector relies on monotone fits, which follow from comparing the same trial against ordered unsigned multiples. When the divisor is zero, every candidate fits and the tree selects digit 15.\n\n## Local validation\n\n- Verilator lint passed in both arithmetic and ALTOPS modes.\n- All six cocotb suites passed, including the divider digit boundaries, widened multiples, signed overflow, divide-by-zero, and held completion.\n- A SAT miter proved that the new and original selectors agree for every monotone fit vector and arbitrary 32-bit candidate words.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks on the first run, including `liveness_ch0` and `reg_ch0`.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and three random programs with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark validated its CRCs and completed 10 iterations in 3,965,757 timed cycles.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 routed at 90.242, 97.408, and 97.408 MHz. Option 0 used 4,662 logic LUTs. The worst paths ended in fetch-queue control. The 97.408 MHz median clears the 95.10 MHz replacement threshold and gives 245.62 CoreMark iterations/s, 7.14% above the champion.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
