{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'\nfor i,l in enumerate(open(p), 1):\n if i in (25,34,37):\n  v=json.loads(l); print('\\\\n',v['id'],v['motivation']); print(v['hypothesis']['hypothesis']); print(v['critical_path']); print(v['implementation_notes'][:2200]);\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261123-003-r8s2 The four-entry fetch queue still spends instruction-bus bandwidth refetching\nevery correctly predicted loop iteration. The champion reproduces 3,965,757\nmarker cycles under both stall sources. Its retirement trace contains about\n1.17 million words in consecutive repeats of contiguous loops of at most 16\nwords. A loop stream detector can keep those iterations fed through imem\nstalls while the existing direction predictor handles the rest of the code.\n\nAdd a single 16-word loop replay buffer in IF. Record consecutive accepted\nbus responses in a circular window indexed by the low four word-PC bits.\nTrack the preceding run of sequential, replayable responses with a shifted\nvalidity mask indexed by the backedge's negative word displacement.\nReset it on redirect, a predicted nonsequential advance, or an excluded\nopcode. Allow straight-line integer, memory, and RV32M opcodes and legal,\naligned conditional branches. Keep jumps, SYSTEM, FENCE, and FENCE.I on\nthe bus path. When a legal, aligned, same-page backward conditional branch\npredicts taken and its complete 2-to-16-word span has been captured, record\nthe head PC and tail slot and enter replay as the branch word is written.\n\nReplay one saved word per cycle with queue space, independent of imem_ready.\nTag each word with its exact PC, predict the internal conditional branches\nnot taken, and predict the tail taken so the replay cursor wraps to the head.\nPark the instruction bus at the loop head and hold the replay curs