{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_94", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r13s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261123-003-r13s2\ntitle: Predict and replay the next fetch through instruction stalls\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,658,045 stalled CoreMark marker cycles at a median\n  99.444 MHz. Its two contiguous loop banks cover about 1.40 million of the\n  2.92 million timed retirement PCs in a trace model. Extending the banks to\n  follow taken branches inside short loops raises modeled coverage to only\n  1.58 million. A 512-row direct-mapped packet table modeled on the same\n  trace matches about 2.82 million PCs. Storing a decoded successor with\n  each completed packet lets fetch keep predicting through instruction-bus\n  stalls across both loop and ordinary control flow.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the closed-loop predictor with a 512-row synchronous successor\n  replay table split into even and odd word-PC banks. Train once per valid,\n  completing MEM instruction. A row contains its full word-PC tag,\n  instruction bits [31:2], the page-local direct target word and bits\n  indicating a predictably aligned conditional branch or JAL. Capture the\n  exact target from EX's direct PC-relative sum, including for a currently\n  untaken branch. Use the existing direction counters with the instruction\n  sign as their cold fallback. A replayed local JAL predicts taken. Other\n  replay packets predict their sequential successor. Train on legal\n  instructions and skip traps, SYSTEM, fences and JALR.\n\n  Read the presented bus request and its sequential successor in parallel.\n  Index each bank by bits [10:3] of its candidate and launch the reads\n  independently of the live branch result and replay hit. The synchronous\n  responses cover both holding a request and advancing sequentially. If a\n  taken transfer moves outside this pair, the bus covers the target until\n  the table can respond. Compare each bank's complete PC tag in parallel.\n  Prefer a ready bus response and retain its fall-through to decode. When\n  the bus stalls, publish a replay packet only on an exact hit with queue\n  space and advance the PC alo\n…[1529 of 4601 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:be5597ffede9f7e7]…\nle: rtl/loop_replay.sv\n    description: Replace loop capture with two synchronous successor banks, parallel full-tag checks, registered collision exclusion and independent resettable validity maps.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Define the MEM training packet and table row containing the exact tag, instruction, local target word and transfer qualifiers.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Register one eligible completion for training and classify exact local targets using the existing EX direct-target sum.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Read the held and sequential requests in parallel. Select payload only from bus readiness, use the hit to qualify queue publication and PC advance, and keep the registered recovery path.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise stall replay across taken and untaken transfers, tag collisions and eviction, queue holds, stalled corrections, and FENCE.I after a code store. Retain exact RVFI continuity and memory side-effect checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
