{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r14s2.yaml; date -u'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261123-003-r14s2\ntitle: Prime instruction replay from the predicted branch target\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion runs canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,379,213 marker\n  cycles at 98.445 MHz. Its two replay banks prime the held and\n  sequential PCs. A taken transfer outside that pair reaches its target\n  before replay can supply the target instruction. The median placement\n  also has a path from replay BRAM through the replay direction and\n  target select into the fetch PC. Moving successor metadata to a\n  parallel distributed RAM preserved the cycle count and moved the\n  median critical path to the divider at 100.805 MHz in a scratch build.\nhypothesis: |\n  Separate replay successor metadata from instruction storage. At every\n  eligible replay write, update a distributed RAM indexed by the same\n  word-PC slot as the instruction. Store the page-local target word,\n  direct transfer qualifiers, and static direction fallback. Read these\n  fields from the registered normal PC. The instruction bank's exact tag,\n  validity, and collision checks qualify both the instruction and the\n  metadata for a stalled fetch. Preserve the ready bus path and the\n  existing bimodal direction policy.\n\n  Add a synchronous target read from a copy of the instruction rows.\n  Launch it from the metadata's target word before direction, bus\n  acceptance, and replay tag checks. Retain the held and sequential\n  reads. On an accepted ordinary taken prediction, register a one-bit\n  preference for the target response on the following cycle. Keep the\n  preference off the target address and derive it from the accepted\n  direction alone. An exact target reply may supply the stalled fetch on\n  that cycle. The regular reads cover subsequent retries. A ready\n  instruction response still takes priority.\n\n  Share the ordinary banks' slot validity with the target copy. At the\n  read edge record whether a same-slot write collides. On admission\n  check the complete PC identity and current validity, and reject a\n  collision. A missed, stale, or aliased target read leaves the fetch\n  waiting for a valid source. Reset and FENCE.I clear availability and\n  suppress writes to the instruction copies and the metadata. Keep\n  recovery-cycle bus behavior, prediction tracking per queued packet,\n  and the existing EX and deferred MEM correction paths.\n\n  A scratch target-read prototype completed the bracket in 3,361,505\n  cycles with all canonical CRCs. With that cycle count, replacement\n  requires a median above 102.44 MHz. The first target-read prototype\n  routed at 92.277 MHz median. Its slowest placement was limited by a\n  late comparison feeding target preference, and its median placement\n  was limited by EX ALU routing. The proposed lookup removes that\n  comparison and a duplicate target-validity lookup. A 103 MHz median\n  at the demonstrated cycle count gives 306.41 iterations/s. Measure both\n  the cycle count and the three-placement median.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/replay_table.sv\n    description: Separate successor metadata into an asynchronous distributed RAM. Mirror the synchronous instruction rows for the early target read, share slot validity, and check the read collision and exact target PC before publishing.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Use parallel successor metadata to steer stalled replay, and register target-response selection from an accepted taken prediction. Keep the existing queue, live fetch, and correction priority.\n  - file: test/test_replay_table.py\n    description: Check first-cycle target replay, incorrect and aliased target reads, same-slot writes to each read source, and reset and FENCE.I invalidation of the copies and metadata.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Stall the first instruction at a predicted taken target across both parities. Exercise a target miss and retry, a full queue, and correction concurrent with a primed target. Check retirement order, exact successor PCs, and wrong-path side effects.\nMon Nov 23 08:17:59 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'trial_dir=/srv/hwebench/tmp/86dd60e1/07d06e73/predictor.EI0DwW\nfor name in sidepack prepack sideboth sidehash; do\n mkdir \"$trial_dir/$name\"\n case \"$name\" in\n  prepack) cp \"$trial_dir/prefetch/\"*.sv \"$trial_dir/$name/\";;\n  *) cp \"$trial_dir/sidecar/\"*.sv \"$trial_dir/$name/\";;\n esac\ndone\npython \"$trial_dir/direction.py\" \"$trial_dir/sidepack\" 6 packed\npython \"$trial_dir/direction.py\" \"$trial_dir/prepack\" 6 packed\npython - \"$trial_dir\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nd=Path(sys.argv[1])\nfor name in ('sidepack','prepack'):\n p=d/name/'if_stage.sv'\n s=p.read_text().replace('direction_trained ? direction_taken : fall_back','branch_direction')\n p.write_text(s)\nfor name in ('sidepack','prepack','sideboth','sidehash'):\n p=d/name/'replay_table.sv'\n s=p.read_text()\n if name in ('sidepack','prepack'):\n  s=s.replace('  output logic fall_back','  output logic fall_back').replace('assign fall_back = successor[0];', 'assign fall_back = 1\\\\'b0;')\n if name in ('sideboth','sidehash'):\n  s=s.replace('logic [12:0] successors [0:511];','logic [12:0] even_successors [0:255], odd_successors [0:255];')\n  a=s.index('  always_ff @(posedge clock)')\n  b=s.index('  localparam integer ROW_WIDTH', a)\n  off='normal_pc[10:3]' if name=='sideboth' else 'normal_pc[10:3] \"'^ normal_pc[18:11]'\"'\n  woff='update.row.pc[10:3]' if name=='sideboth' else 'update.row.pc[10:3] \"'^ update.row.pc[18:11]'\"'\n  s=s[:a]+f'''  logic [12:0] training_successor;\n  assign training_successor = {{update.row.packet.target_word, update.row.packet.branch,\n                               update.row.packet.jal, update.row.packet.instr[31]}};\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (write_even)\n      even_successors[{woff}] <= training_successor;\n    if (write_odd)\n      odd_successors[{woff}] <= training_successor;\n  end\n\n  assign successor = normal_pc[2] ? odd_successors[{off}] : even_successors[{off}];\n'''+s[b:]\n # A hash must select the same location as the instruction banks and their valid map.\n if name=='sidehash':\n  s=s.replace('normal_pc[10:3] + {7\\\\'b0, normal_pc[2]}', '(normal_pc[10:3] + {7\\\\'b0, normal_pc[2]}) \"'^ (normal_pc[18:11] + {7'\"\\\\'b0, &normal_pc[10:2]})')\n  s=s.replace('= normal_pc[10:3];','= normal_pc[10:3] \"'^ normal_pc[18:11];'\"').replace('= update.row.pc[10:3];','= update.row.pc[10:3] \"'^ update.row.pc[18:11];'\"')\n p.write_text(s)\n\nfor name in ('dir128','dir256'):\n p=d/name/'if_stage.sv'\n s=p.read_text()\n for which in ('read','write'):\n  import re\n  s=re.sub(rf'rear_{which}_q\\\\[\\\\d+:0\\\\]',f'rear_{which}_q[1:0]',s)\n p.write_text(s)\nPY\nfor v in sidepack prepack sideboth sidehash; do\n   PYTHONPATH=\\\"\"'$PWD\" PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python \"$trial_dir/time_variant.py\" \"$v\" > \"$trial_dir/${v}_timing.log\" &\n   (\n    MAKEFLAGS=-j4 RTL_DIR=\"$trial_dir/$v\" OBJ_DIR=\"$trial_dir/${v}_obj\" NRET=1 bash test/cosim/build.sh >\"$trial_dir/${v}_build.log\" 2>&1\n    cd \"$trial_dir\" && ./${v}_obj/cosim_sim coremark.elf 10000000 --bench --istall --dstall > \"${v}.json\"\n   ) &\ndone\nwait\ncat \"$trial_dir\"/{sidepack,prepack,sideboth,sidehash}_timing.log'", "aggregated_output": "0 88.587 None {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/divisor_q_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.288, 'arrival_ns': 16.586, 'logic_cells': 16, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\n1 89.27 None {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/divisor_q_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.202, 'arrival_ns': 16.5, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\n2 89.27 None {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/divisor_q_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.202, 'arrival_ns': 16.5, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\n{'placement_failed': False, 'fmax_mhz': 89.27, 'seeds': [88.587, 89.27, 89.2