{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'GOWIN|cosim|COREMARK' Makefile && rg --files cores/bench/test && cat formal/checks_si.cfg\"","aggregated_output":"1:.PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n19:#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n31:COREMARK ?=\n41:ifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n42:  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\n53:CORE_TARGETS := lint test cosim cosim-build formal formal-deep fpga next loop\n79:\t@echo \"  make cosim TARGET=v1    — RVFI cosim against Python ISS\"\n112:cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\n113:\tpython3 -m tools.eval.cosim . $(TARGET)\n115:cosim-build: $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv) test/cosim/main.cpp\n116:\tbash test/cosim/build.sh\n137:fpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\n168:\t  $(if $(strip $(COREMARK)),COREMARK=$(COREMARK),) \\\n178:\trm -rf test/cosim/sim_build sim_build out\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
